upil appears larger than the left and reacts sluggishly to bright light.","He exhibits weaker spontaneous movement of the left arm and leg compared with the right.","His breathing pattern is irregular, punctuated by short apneic spells.","A rigid cervical collar is in place and breath sounds are clear bilaterally."]},{"sid":46518,"type":"plan","lines":["Rapid sequence endotracheal intubation is performed.","The team initiates controlled hyperventilation per protocol.","The head of the bed is elevated and sedation is started.","Shortly afterward, the pupillary asymmetry appears slightly less pronounced.","Neurosurgery is en route for emergent intervention.","While preparing for imaging, the senior resident reviews why the ventilator strategy can transiently lower intracranial pressure.","She asks the medical student to explain the key physiologic effect of lowering arterial carbon dioxide in this setting."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":11068,"date":"2023-05-15","type":"icu","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. James Park","cc":"Fall from 10-foot height onto concrete surface with altered mental status.","order":3,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[6786],"sections":[{"sid":46519,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Fall from 10-foot height onto concrete surface with altered mental status."]},{"sid":46520,"type":"hpi","lines":["This 34-year-old male with a history of post-traumatic central diabetes insipidus and epilepsy secondary to multiple prior traumatic brain injuries presents after a fall.","On arrival, he is confused but able to answer simple questions."]},{"sid":46521,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Central diabetes insipidus (inadequately controlled) (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Acute Epidural Hematoma (diagnosed 2020-09-15)","- Traumatic brain injury (diagnosed 2021-11-15)","- Post-traumatic central diabetes insipidus","- Post-traumatic epilepsy","- Alcohol use disorder, severe","- Chronic pain syndrome"]},{"sid":46522,"type":"psh","lines":["- Crani